We used to have a kwarg transform that you can pass a element-wise function to do a transform on the mcmc sample:
pm.traceplot(short_trace, var_names=['tau'], transform=np.log);
Not sure if this is still a useful feature, if so we should add it to arviz, if not we should remove all the reference to it in our doc and modify those plotting accordingly.
@ColCarroll @canyon289 @aloctavodia

I installed from the master repo.  Here is __init__ signature for NormalMixture:
def __init__(self, w, mu, comp_shape=(), *args, **kwargs)
In a previous version, I was able to use NormalMixture('name', w, mu, sigma) but now this breaks. I think it would be more consistent with the rest of the library (and the order in which parameters are documented) if sigma was given as an explicit keyword argument, after mu.
